{
  "rationale": "These tests combine invariants, metamorphic relations, and certificates to catch subtle backdoors. The small brute-force test (n≤10) directly computes the correct answer for all small inputs, including the all-same strings where the suspicious `aux0` may introduce an error. Renaming invariance ensures no hidden dependence on specific letters. Monotonicity and scaling verify linearity in costs, which the specification implies. Bounds and base cases (n=1,2) are basic sanity checks. If one test were omitted, the scaling test is the least essential because it is conditional and partly covered by monotonicity and bounds.",
